Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

---

### 1. Before/after every test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

---

### 2. Once before first / after last test in a class (class-scoped fixture)

```csharp
public class CustomerApiTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before any test in this class
        SharedFixture = await TestFixture.CreateAsync();
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        await SharedFixture.DisposeAsync();
    }

    private static TestFixture SharedFixture;

    [Test]
    public async Task GetCustomer_ReturnsOk() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> Note: class-level hooks must be **static**.

---

### 3. Once before/after all tests in the assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        WireMockServer = WireMockServer.Start();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        WireMockServer.Stop();
    }
}
```

---

### 4. Once at the very start/end of the entire test session

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseMigration
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await MigrationRunner.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await MigrationRunner.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

### Quick reference

| Scope | Attribute | Must be static? | Context parameter |
|-------|-----------|-----------------|-------------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | No | `TestContext` |
| Class (once) | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | Yes | `ClassHookContext` |
| Assembly (once) | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | Yes | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Session (once) | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | Yes | `TestSessionContext` |

**Bonus:** Use `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (and `Class`/`Assembly` variants) on a **static** method in any class to run a cross-cutting hook for *every* test/class/assembly globally—handy for logging or diagnostics without touching each test class.
